# 5. NPM (Node Package Manager)

## Definition

Node Package Manager (NPM) is a package manager for JavaScript.

Used for:

* Installing libraries
* Managing dependencies
* Updating packages

---

## Important Notes

Google developed Angular and Node.js uses NPM.

NPM is common for both Angular and Node.js.

Before working with Angular:

### Install Node.js First

Because Angular depends on NPM.

---

## Node Modules Folder

The node_modules folder stores all downloaded packages and libraries from NPM.

