# 7. Components

Components are the fundamental building blocks of Angular applications.

A component is a self-contained unit that encapsulates:

* User Interface
* Business Logic
* Behavior

Components are the most basic UI building blocks of an Angular application.

---

## Component Files

### app.component.ts

Main TypeScript file.

Responsible for linking all component files together.

---

### app.component.html

Contains HTML template.

Used for designing the UI.

---

### app.component.css

Contains component-specific CSS.

Used for styling.

---

### app.component.spec.ts

Contains Unit Test cases.

Used for testing components.

---

# 8. Modules

Modules group related:

* Components
* Directives
* Pipes
* Services

into cohesive blocks of functionality.

---

## Characteristics of Modules

### 1. Grouping

Organizes related functionality together.

---

### 2. Dependency Management

Declares dependencies on other modules.

Ensures required functionality is available.

---

### 3. Scalability

Makes applications easier to expand and maintain.

---

### 4. Lazy Loading

Loads modules only when needed.

Benefits:

* Better performance
* Faster initial loading

