# 10. Bootstrapped Module vs Bootstrapped Component

## Bootstrapped Module

### Definition

A module is a cohesive block of code dedicated to:

* Application domain
* Workflow
* Related capabilities

Usually:

```text
AppModule
```

acts as the Root Module.

---

### Angular Module (NgModule)

A class marked with:

```typescript
@NgModule
```

decorator.

---

### Bootstrap Array

Specifies which component should be loaded when application starts.

Example:

```typescript
bootstrap: [AppComponent]
```

---

## Bootstrapped Component

### Definition

The root component Angular inserts into index.html.

Usually:

```text
AppComponent
```

---

### Component Decorator

Root component uses:

```typescript
@Component
```

decorator.

Defines:

* Selector
* Template
* Styles

