# 11. Data Binding

Data Binding synchronizes data between:

* Model
* View

---

## 11.1 String Interpolation

### Purpose

Displays component data in UI.

### Syntax

```html
{{ propertyName }}
```

### Example

```html
<h1>{{ title }}</h1>
```

```typescript
title = "Welcome to Angular";
```

---

## 11.2 Property Binding

### Purpose

Binds values to HTML properties.

### Syntax

```html
[property]="expression"
```

### Example

```html
<img [src]="imageUrl">
```

```typescript
imageUrl = "path/to/image.jpg";
```

---

## 11.3 Event Binding

### Purpose

Handles user actions.

Examples:

* Click
* Key Press
* Mouse Events

### Syntax

```html
(event)="method()"
```

### Example

```html
<button (click)="onClick()">
Click Me
</button>
```

```typescript
onClick() {
   alert("Button clicked!");
}
```

---

## 11.4 Two-Way Data Binding

### Purpose

Synchronizes data both ways.

* Component → View
* View → Component

Uses:

```html
ngModel
```

### Syntax

```html
[(ngModel)]="property"
```

### Example

```html
<input [(ngModel)]="name">
<p>Hello, {{name}}!</p>
```

```typescript
name = "";
```

