# 12. Directives

Directives are classes that add additional behavior to elements in an application.

---

# 12.1 Component Directives

Components are a special type of directive with a template.

They control a portion of the screen called a View.

---

# 12.2 Structural Directives

Structural Directives change the DOM layout by:

* Adding elements
* Removing elements
* Manipulating elements

Usually start with:

```html
*
```

---

## Common Structural Directives

### *ngIf

Conditionally adds/removes elements.

Changes appearance of DOM by adding and removing elements.

---

### *ngFor

Repeats template for each item in a collection.

---

### *ngSwitch

Changes DOM structure based on matching expression.

---

# 12.3 Attribute Directives

Attribute Directives change:

* Appearance
* Behavior

without changing DOM structure.

---

## Common Attribute Directives

### ngClass

Adds or removes CSS classes.

Changes appearance or behavior of elements.

---

### ngStyle

Adds or removes styles.

Changes appearance or behavior of elements.

---

### ngModel

Binds:

* input
* select
* textarea

to component properties.

---

# 13. Directive Comparison

| Component Directives                     | Structural Directives                             | Attribute Directives                        |
| ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |
| Responsible for showing first whole view | Responsible for adding and deleting HTML elements | Responsible for changing appearance of view |
| Most commonly used                       | Changes DOM structure                             | Changes styles and behavior                 |
| Starts with @                            | Starts with *                                     | Used inside []                              |
| Example: Component                       | Example: *ngIf, *ngFor, *ngSwitch                 | Example: [ngClass], [ngStyle]               |

